    "body": "Currently, a local account can be linked with a federated account via the dashboard without actually having access to that federated account.\r\n\r\nThis can cause issues if the user misspells, or otherwise incorrectly enters, their federated account name.  A user should be required to prove that they have access to both accounts before they can be linked (similarly to the way linking a local account already requires the other account's password).\r\n\r\nThe most serious intentional misuse of this function I can think of offhand is to self-register a bunch of accounts and then link them all to another user's federated account, which could cause confusion for that user.  I haven't thoroughly explored how permissions might be shared with federated accounts at this point, but that could certainly be an area of concern as well.",
